  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 123 PM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nRidging stays over South Central Texas and strengthens midweek with \ndry weather continuing, allowing highs to inch a little higher with \nmore of the I-35 corridor, Coastal Plains, and Rio Grande Plains \ngetting into the upper 80s. The bulk of the heat accompanying the \nridge should remain centered over northern Mexico and West Texas, so \nhighs are expected to plateau mid to late week. We will gradually\ntrade out lows in the 50s for lows in the 60s during the week as \nthe ridge encourages more onshore flow and slightly higher \nmoisture.\n\nThe next atmospheric of disturbance of interest comes in the form of \na trough progressing over the western US this weekend. Our overhead \nridging favors this troughing being deflected to the north away from \nthe area. This in turn keeps rain chances low (below 25 percent for \nmost areas), but a few isolated rains are possible along the low-\nlevel response to the approaching trough, mainly along the Rio \nGrande and Edwards Plateau Sunday into Monday. Otherwise, most of \nSouth Central Texas is forecast to remain devoid of raid for the \nnext seven days. Daytime temperatures this upcoming weekend are very \nlikely (above 90%) to remain above 80F. Lows should continue to be \nin the upper 50s to mid 60s.",
